{
  "name": "Onboarding Chase and Evidence",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## What this does\n\nEight new clients owe the practice paperwork. Every weekday morning this looks\nat where each one stands and decides **one thing per client**: nudge them, leave\nthem alone, or hand them to a person.\n\nIt runs again tomorrow and decides again. **Nothing waits inside the workflow.**\n\nToday: three nudged, one closed off, one escalated, three deliberately left\nalone - and every one of those decisions is written down.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "e8000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1900,
        -460
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Why there is no Wait node\n\nThe obvious build is: send the request, **Wait** three days, send a reminder,\n**Wait** four more. One tidy line on the canvas.\n\nIt is a trap. That execution sits open for a fortnight, and any n8n restart,\nupgrade or crash silently loses every pending chase. Nobody finds out until a\nclient says they were never contacted - and by then there is no record of what\nhappened, which in a regulated practice is worse than the missed chase.\n\n**The workflow stays stateless. The tracker is what is stateful.** A schedule\nre-reads the truth every morning and decides fresh. It survives a restart\nbecause there is nothing in flight to lose.\n\nThe weekend rule is not a node either - it is the cron expression on the\ntrigger, `0 9 * * 1-5`.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "e8000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1400,
        -460
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Evidence, not status\n\n`Record What Happened` is **append-only**. Nothing in it is ever updated,\nbecause a row that can be edited is not evidence.\n\nNote what gets recorded: **the decisions not to act.** \"Considered, not chased,\nbecause they replied yesterday\" is a row. A silent gap in the log looks\nidentical to nobody bothering, and that is the difference between an activity\nlog and something a supervisory body will accept.\n\nA status field tells you where you are. An audit trail tells you how you got\nthere. Only the second one survives an inspection.\n\n**Four nodes are greyed out** - nothing sends, closes or records until you\nswitch them on.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 470,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "e8000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Note 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -880,
        -460
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 9 * * 1-5"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
