    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Write one short reminder email to a client of Ashcombe & Partners who\nstill owes us onboarding paperwork.\n\ncontact first name: {{ $json.contact_name.split(' ')[0] }}\nstill outstanding: {{ $json.outstanding }}\nalready received: {{ $json.received }}\nthis is reminder number: {{ $json.chase_number }}\ndays since we first asked: {{ $json.days_since_request }}\nupload link: https://portal.ashcombe.example/upload/{{ $json.client_id }}\nsign off as: {{ $json.account_owner }}\n\nRules:\n- Name every outstanding item, exactly as listed above. Never ask for anything already received,\n  and open by thanking them for what has come in when the list is not empty.\n- Reminder 1 is light. Reminder 2 notes the delay plainly. Reminder 3 explains the real reason\n  we keep asking: we are required to complete client due diligence before any work can begin on\n  their affairs, so nothing can move forward until the documents are with us. That is a fact,\n  not a threat - write it as one.\n- Never invent a deadline, a fee, a penalty or a consequence that was not agreed.\n- Offer one easy next step: the upload link, and an invitation to say if something is holding\n  it up.\n- Under 120 words. No exclamation marks, no chasing language like \"urgent\" or \"final notice\".\n  Write the way a practice writes to a client it wants to keep.\n- Return the body only, with no subject line.",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": []
        }
      },
      "id": "e8000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012",
      "name": "Write the Reminder",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.4,
      "position": [
        -740,
        120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "sendTo": "={{ $('What Does the Policy Say?').item.json.contact_email }}",
        "subject": "=Outstanding paperwork for your {{ $('What Does the Policy Say?').item.json.client_name }} onboarding",
        "emailType": "text",
        "message": "={{ $json.text }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "e8000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013",
